&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Luna-Bondreader: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name, write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/luna. Handback to /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/luna/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 1400 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. No git writes, no suites. Web allowed; cite URLs. Code: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine (span head, read only).

WAVE TWO (the ratchet). Common brief: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/brief-common.md. Your wave one:
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/luna/own-wave1.md. Your peer's: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/luna/peer-wave1.md. Read all three, then the code again where you split.

You agree: retire the vessel-wide Keyhive Individual and the place ContactCard as general peer proof; every face
operation (dial, join, edge, enrolment, sibling, daemon proof, group-secret open, internal face ask, meme promotion)
signs or opens by the selected face's atom under its FCK; a faceless vessel signs only its five floor duties under the
scoped place signer and refuses face work; old mixed archives refuse by name (no CRDT document survives until X0, so
re-genesis replaces migration). The controller reads these as settled by house law, not operator questions:
* The relay key: road :207 says an S row's "principal and opener the house names row by row", so a random relay-only S
row with the relay service as principal falls to the house (no sixth place duty).
* Face selection: "A command names its face" and the session-wears-the-face ruling already require an explicit face and
refuse ambiguity (I1's CLI takes &#45;-face N).
* Internal asks: classify per call by its protected relation; no shared S key.
Contest any of these only with a measured reason. Settle:
F1. THE FACELESS CARRIER'S SUBSTRATE NEED. Does a faceless herm or floor-only node need ANY Keyhive identity to sync or
carry documents (automerge-repo peer id, Keyhive/Beelay sync auth, the share policy, the carriage board's writer)?
MEASURE the herm's sync path and the share policy (grep peerId, sharePolicy, Individual, beelay in mesh/node/keyhive).
If one stands, name what replaces it (a random per-vessel carriage identity in an S or F row? a public place id?)
without making it a shared secret or a face link.
F2. THE CENSUS'S BLIND SPOTS. Sol warned the token matcher catches selected spellings. Trace TRANSITIVE consumers: every
caller that receives a value derived from the vessel seed (vesselKey, vesselSigner, keypair.secretKey, device key)
through a parameter, not by name. List each, file:line, and whether the census sees it.
F3. THE CUT. One lane or several? Name the slices in build order, each with files, its reds (the place-seed thief, the
controls, the known positives), and which hunks go as patches to W14-W16 (floor pins, card, nexus-contract), D2
(open-node-vessel port hunks) and G15 (afterRollChain). Say which slice moves identity bytes and must precede X0.
F4. THE OPERATOR LIST: only what survives F1-F3 and the three settled points, each with options and one lean.

